eight=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fwe-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out%2Fcover.webp"/><link rel="icon" href="/static/favicon.png"/><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Ubuntu+Mono&amp;family=Lato:wght@100;900&amp;family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,300&amp;display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/><script>try{if(localStorage.getItem('authToken')){document.documentElement.classList.add('auth-pending');}}catch(e){}</script><script src="/_next/static/chunks/polyfills-42372ed130431b0a.js" noModule=""></script></head><body><noscript><iframe src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-WRN9GT5R" height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript><div class="bg-dark fixed-top"><div class="container"><nav class="navbar navbar-expand-md navbar-dark"><div class="container-fluid padding-left-0 padding-right-0"><a class="navbar-brand" href="/"><img src="/static/logo_header_black.png" width="160" height="40" class="margin-right-20" alt="TeckDeck.io logo"/></a><button class="navbar-toggler" type="button" aria-label="Menu Button"><span class="navbar-toggler-icon"></span></button><div class="collapse navbar-collapse " id="navbarText"><ul class="navbar-nav me-auto mb-2 mb-lg-0"><li><a class="nav-link px-2 margin-right-20 text-white link-orange" href="/tags">Tags</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link px-2 margin-right-20 text-white link-orange" href="/sources">Sources</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a class="nav-link px-2 margin-right-20 text-white link-orange" href="/contact">Contact</a></li></ul><ul class="navbar-nav"><li class="nav-item"><a href="/login" class="nav-link px-2 margin-right-20 text-white link-orange">Login</a></li><li class="nav-item"><a href="/register" class="join-nav-link margin-right-5">Join</a></li></ul></div></div></nav></div></div><div class="container margin-top-80"><div class="margin-top-20"><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"NewsArticle","headline":"We stopped reading 2,195 MCP servers for three days. Another team's log is how we found out","description":"Explore how a logging issue in HISTOR affected server readings and what was learned to avoid future pitfalls.","image":"https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1200,height=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fwe-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out%2Fcover.webp","datePublished":"2026-11-02","dateModified":"2026-11-02T05:36:47.888507","keywords":["data monitoring","logging","mcp servers","server management","team collaboration"],"isBasedOn":"https://dev.to/alexar76/we-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out-52g0","mainEntityOfPage":"https://teckdeck.io/posts/we-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-team-s-log-is-how-we-found-out","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TeckDeck.io","url":"https://teckdeck.io"},"publisher":{"@type":"Organization","name":"TeckDeck.io","url":"https://teckdeck.io"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What caused the disruption in server reads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A change in the MCP session initiation process led to compatibility issues, causing HISTOR to fail in reading data from 2,195 servers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How was the problem eventually detected?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The issue was identified by comparing logs from HISTOR with a new log system called ScraperWatch, which showed discrepancies."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What actions were taken to resolve the issue?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The reading system was updated to better handle protocol versions and errors, allowing it to recover from the failure."}}]}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://teckdeck.io"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Data monitoring","item":"https://teckdeck.io/tags/tag-data-monitoring"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"We stopped reading 2,195 MCP servers for three days. Another team's log is how we found out"}]}</script><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-9 col-md-12 col-sm-12"><article class="element-base post-page margin-bottom-20 fade-in"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="font-size-14 text-mid-gray"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tags/tag-data-monitoring">Data monitoring</a></nav><div class="post-page-meta font-size-14"><img src="/media/source_images/dev_to.webp" height="16" width="16" alt=""/><a href="/sources/dev-to-engineering-portal" class="text-orange"><b>dev.to</b></a><time dateTime="2026-11-02" class="text-mid-gray">2 Nov 2026</time></div><h1 class="post-page-title">We stopped reading 2,195 MCP servers for three days. Another team&#x27;s log is how we found out</h1><div class="post-page-tags"><a href="/tags/tag-data-monitoring"><span class="badge-tag badge rounded-pill">data monitoring</span></a><a href="/tags/tag-logging"><span class="badge-tag badge rounded-pill">logging</span></a><a href="/tags/tag-mcp-servers"><span class="badge-tag badge rounded-pill">mcp servers</span></a><a href="/tags/tag-server-management"><span class="badge-tag badge rounded-pill">server management</span></a><a href="/tags/tag-team-collaboration"><span class="badge-tag badge rounded-pill">team collaboration</span></a></div><a href="https://dev.to/alexar76/we-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out-52g0" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary post-page-cta">Read the full article on <!-- -->dev.to</a><img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=1200,height=627,fit=cover,gravity=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fmodelmarket.dev%2Fblog%2Fwe-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out%2Fcover.webp" alt="We stopped reading 2,195 MCP servers for three days. Another team&#x27;s log is how we found out" class="img-fluid post-page-image"/><section class="post-page-tldr"><h2 class="post-page-label">TL;DR</h2><p>HISTOR, a tool reading MCP servers, stopped receiving data from 2,195 servers for three days. This failure went undetected until an overlapping log revealed the issue. The article discusses the technical causes and offers insights for MCP client development.</p></section><section><h2 class="post-page-heading">Key points</h2><ul><li>HISTOR&#x27;s failure went unnoticed due to high success rates in server reads, obscuring the 2,195 inactive servers.</li><li>The MCP revision changed the session initiation process, leading to compatibility issues.</li><li>A new logging tool, ScraperWatch, helped detect the problem by contrasting its findings with HISTOR&#x27;s.</li></ul></section><section><h2 class="post-page-heading">Quick facts</h2><dl class="post-page-facts"><div><dt>Affected Servers</dt><dd>2,195</dd></div><div><dt>Fix Implemented</dt><dd>November 1 at 08:44:57 UTC</dd></div><div><dt>Success Rate Before Fix</dt><dd>98.8% on 9,514 reads</dd></div><div><dt>Protocol Speaking Servers</dt><dd>19% spoke the new protocol as of November 1</dd></div><div><dt>Comparison Tool</dt><dd>ScraperWatch</dd></div></dl></section><section><h2 class="post-page-heading">Why it matters</h2><p>This scenario highlights the importance of effective logging and monitoring systems in tech environments, demonstrating how overlapping data sources can reveal issues that otherwise remain hidden. It serves as a lesson for developers about backward compatibility and the need for robust error handling in clients.</p></section><section><h2 class="post-page-heading">Who it&#x27;s for</h2><p>Developers and engineers working with MCP clients and network protocol systems should find this article particularly relevant.</p></section><section><h2 class="post-page-heading">FAQ</h2><details class="post-page-faq" open=""><summary>What caused the disruption in server reads?</summary><p>A change in the MCP session initiation process led to compatibility issues, causing HISTOR to fail in reading data from 2,195 servers.</p></details><details class="post-page-faq"><summary>How was the problem eventually detected?</summary><p>The issue was identified by comparing logs from HISTOR with a new log system called ScraperWatch, which showed discrepancies.</p></details><details class="post-page-faq"><summary>What actions were taken to resolve the issue?</summary><p>The reading system was updated to better handle protocol versions and errors, allowing it to recover from the failure.</p></details></section><p class="post-page-disclaimer font-size-14 text-mid-gray">Summary written by TeckDeck.io from the original article on <!-- -->dev.to<!-- -->. All rights to the original content belong to its author.<!-- --> <a href="https://dev.to/alexar76/we-stopped-reading-2195-mcp-servers-for-three-days-another-teams-log-is-how-we-found-out-52g0" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the original</a>.</p></article></div><aside class="col-lg-3 col-md-12 col-sm-12"><div class="element-base sticky-top post-page-related fade-in"><h2 class="post-page-label">More on <!-- -->Data monitoring</h2><a href="/posts/12-hidden-mcp-servers-that-are-actually-useful" class="post-page-related-item">12 Hidden MCP Servers That Are Actually Useful<small class="text-mid-gray">dev.to<!-- --> · 9 Nov 2026</small></a><a href="/posts/show-hn-replay-your-claude-code-logs-to-count-parallel-session-collisions" class="post-page-related-item">Show HN: Replay your Claude Code logs to count parallel session collisions<small class="text-mid-gray">github.com<!-- --> · 9 Nov 2026</small></a><a href="/posts/all-in-term-all-in-one-terminal-server-management-for-macos" class="post-page-related-item">All in Term – All-in-One Terminal &amp; Server Management for macOS<small class="text-mid-gray">dev.to<!-- --> · 8 Nov 2026</small></a><a href="/posts/i-deleted-plan-md-my-ai-agent-now-plans-logs-and-proves-its-work-in-one-file" class="post-page-related-item">I deleted plan.md. My AI agent now plans, logs and proves its work in one file.<small class="text-mid-gray">dev.to<!-- --> · 8 Nov 2026</small></a><a href="/tags/tag-data-monitoring" class="text-orange">All posts tagged <!-- -->data monitoring</a><a href="/sources/dev-to-engineering-portal" class="text-orange post-page-source-link">All posts from <!-- -->dev.to<img src="/media/source_images/dev_to.webp" height="16" width="16" alt=""/></a></div></aside></div></div></div><div class="footer-app"><div class="container"><div class="row"><div class="col-lg-3 col-md-12 col-sm-12 ms-auto" align="center"><div align="center" class="margin-bottom-10 margin-top-10"><a href="https://t.me/teckdeck_io" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="d-inline-block"><div class="social-image-telegram"></div></a></div><div class="margin-bottom-10"><a href="https://startupbase.io/products/teckdeck-io?utm_source=startupbase&amp;utm_medium=badge&amp;utm_campaign=launch-badge-neutral" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="d-inline-block"><img src="https://statics.startupbase.io/site/badges/launched-on-sb-neutral.svg" alt="Launched on StartupBase" height="55" style="height:55px;width:auto"/></a></div><nav class="footer-links margin-bottom-10" aria-label="Footer"><a href="/contact" class="custom-link-white">Contact</a></nav><b>TeckDeck.io</b> (c) <!-- -->2026<!-- --> created by Oleg Klimenko</div></div></div></div><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-61495c061f6f6888.js" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\"]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/fd514dda8be8d232.css\",\"style\"]\n"])</script><scr